*  g-cn2 (T2 half) -- WHY THE T2 FOLD IS NOT REACHABLE FROM A FRAGMENT,
*  pinned so the day it BECOMES reachable is a gate event and not a
*  silent one.
*  T2 folds at *&Name DEFER sites in pattern position.  EVAL('*&Word')
*  raises Error 22 today -- the deferred-expression construct is outside
*  the fragment-compilable subset -- so the fold site cannot be reached
*  from a runtime fragment at all.  What a fragment CAN do is read the
*  constant by name, and that must reach the SEALED CELL: a pattern-
*  valued constant is not a T1 site either (T1 admits only ILIT/FLIT/
*  QLIT), so both tiers decline and the by-name route is the answer.
*  ⛔ IF THE FRAGMENT SUBSET EVER WIDENS TO ADMIT *&Name, the g-cn2
*  clear of g_sno_seal_enabled in sno_lower_fragment_at stops being
*  prophylactic and becomes the thing standing between T2 and the
*  cross-compile pointer hazard that broke T1.  Do not remove it as
*  "unused" -- this witness is the reason it looks unused.
*  ORACLE_FAIL BY CONSTRUCTION: stock sbl 251s every &-prefixed user name.
	&USER_DECLARED_CONSTANTS = 1
	&Word = SPAN('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz')
	'hello42' ? *&Word . W				:F(N1)
	OUTPUT = 'direct=' W
N1	OUTPUT = 'eval-dt=' EVAL('DATATYPE(&Word)')
	P = EVAL('&Word')
	'zebra9' ? P . V				:F(N2)
	OUTPUT = 'eval-byname=' V			:(END)
N2	OUTPUT = 'EVAL-BYNAME-NOMATCH'
END
